Reading SRTR codes
sRtr labels coded values as “code: meaning”. This function returns the numeric code from either form, so code lists can be matched against the SRTR formats whether or not the labels have been applied.


Click to show/hide R Code
# The numeric code of an SRTR value. sRtr::load_srtr_file() labels coded
# values as "&lt;code&gt;: &lt;meaning&gt;" (for example "3011: KI:DIABETES ..."); this
# returns 3011 whether the value is labelled or still a number.
srtr_code &lt;- function(x) {
  if (is.numeric(x)) {
    return(as.numeric(x))
  }
  x |&gt;
    as.character() |&gt;
    stringr::str_extract("^-?[0-9]+") |&gt;
    as.numeric()
}


